14:13:39 said  I decompiled the original's branch placement code and rebuilt the app to follow it. The build passes Craft Anything's check, including the self-test.
14:13:39 said  **What the original actually does, and what changed:**
14:13:39 said  - **Classic mode:** the number of branches is Frequency with any fraction dropped. Each branch lands at a random height between First and Last; before, I spaced them evenly with a little jitter. How far each one turns around the parent is controlled by the original's own settings, so the panel now has Balanced, Offset, Sweep and Roll in place of my "spiral step" and "roll variance". There is also a new Relative style, where the count is parent length × Frequency × 0.025.
14:13:39 said  - **Absolute mode:** branches are spread evenly around the parent with a bit of random wobble, then centred.
14:13:39 said  - **Interval mode:** it walks down the parent from Last in steps of 10 ÷ Frequency, putting a set number of branches at each step. Its Spiral setting adds a little extra turn at each step.
14:13:39 said  - **Slider limits:** several now come from the original's own property tables. For example, start angle runs 0 to 1, Roll runs −1 to 1, and jink runs 0 to 1.
14:13:39 said  These rules and their code locations are written into the values sheet, which now lists 37 values traced to the original and 15 still estimated.
14:13:39 said  **Still estimated:**
14:13:39 said  - **How a branch bends** (gravity, wobble, sudden kinks) and **how it thins toward the tip.** I couldn't find the code that applies them, because it doesn't refer to those settings by name. Those rules are still my own approximation.
14:13:39 said  - **Exact tree shapes.** The original draws its random numbers from a built-in table; I use my own generator, so the same seed won't give an identical tree.
14:13:39 said  - **Phyllotaxy mode** reuses the Interval walk, because I didn't decompile the original's version.
14:13:39 said  - **Inside the material and mesh editors.** I couldn't see them in the running original, so those layouts are still my design.
14:13:39 said  A good next step would be to ask me to keep tracing the branch-bending code, which would make the shapes closer to the original's.
