03:08:56 said  I decompiled the rest of the original's Meshes panel and changed four things to match it:
03:08:56 said  - **Duplicate:** the copy is now named "… Copy" (with the original's numbering when that name is taken) and added at the end of the list.
03:08:56 said  - **Loading a file over a cutout:** you're now asked first whether you really want to replace the mesh's own data.
03:08:56 said  - **Loading a High file:** TreeCraft now offers to find matching "…LOD1", "…LOD2" files in the same folder and fill Med and Low with them. It only reads OBJ files; the original also looks for its other mesh formats.
03:08:56 said  - **Count label:** it now reads like the original's, for example "V:27 F:32 A:1".
03:08:56 said  One difference remains: in the original, Edit Mesh… on a mesh loaded from a file converts it so it can be edited. TreeCraft can only edit cutouts, so it offers "Replace with a cutout" instead.
03:08:57 said  These rules are in the values sheet. A new test checks the LOD file search, and the app builds and passes Craft Anything's check.
